      "description": "This sculpture of an Acadian family was commissioned to mark the 250th anniversary of the tragic deportation of thousands of Acadians from their ancestral homeland between 1755 and 1762. The family symbolizes the experiences of the numerous families that were forcibly uprooted from their homes and sent into exile to face the unknown future in foreign lands.\nQuebec artists Jules LaSalle and Andre Fournelle created the sculpture, which was unveiled on September 3, 2006.",
